-- Q2597: Like-Kind Exchanges [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 1031 and Treas. Reg. Sec. 1.1031(k)-1(g)(4), a qualified intermediary facilitates a deferred like-kind exchange by holding sale proceeds from the relinquished property and using them to acquire replacement property on behalf of the taxpayer. This prevents constructive receipt of funds that would disqualify the exchange.
Wrong (A): Appraisal is performed by licensed appraisers, not by a qualified intermediary whose role is transactional facilitation.
Wrong (B): Tax advice is provided by CPAs or tax attorneys; the QI''s function is holding proceeds and executing the exchange.
Wrong (C): The QI acts on behalf of the taxpayer, not the IRS; the IRS has no representative role in like-kind exchanges.$EXPL$
