Wrong (A): Using the gross mortgage relief of $150,000 ignores the offsetting $90,000 mortgage assumed, which must be netted per the regulations.
Wrong (B): The $90,000 mortgage assumed is an offset to boot, not the boot itself; boot is the net excess of relief over assumption.
