  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 1031(f), a like-kind exchange between related parties is disqualified if either party disposes of the exchanged property within two years. This anti-abuse rule prevents related parties from using exchanges to shift basis and then cash out.
Wrong (A): Exchanging an office building for raw land qualifies because both are real property held for investment or business use under Sec. 1031(a).
Wrong (B): Using a qualified intermediary for a deferred exchange is an accepted method under Treas. Reg. Sec. 1.1031(k)-1(g)(4).
